# Python bytecode / build
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Test / lint / type caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.grimp_cache/

# archmap: graph.json IS committed (the diffable architecture artifact); the interactive viewer shell is
# regenerated (template-identical, ~700KB of vendored libs) locally / in the Pages workflow — not committed.
docs/architecture/index.html

# Virtualenv. `.venv-arm/` is the SECOND one, and it exists because a shared environment is mutable
# state that a forty-minute run holds open: every pre-commit entry is `uv run --extra dev|devtools`, and
# alternating extras makes uv rewrite `.venv` in place — under the interpreter an arm is already using.
# That killed a run on 2026-08-13 (mid epoch 4) and again on 2026-08-20 (mid epoch 1, step 182), both
# times as exit 127 with no traceback. `--no-sync` stops the ARM from syncing; it cannot stop a push
# from syncing underneath it. Arms therefore run against their own environment.
.venv/
.venv-arm/

# Logs / local DBs — anchored to root (`/logs/`, not `logs/`, so a source dir named logs/ isn't ignored)
/logs/
*.db

# External git-repo deps: checked out under external/, never vendored. Anchored — a package may
# legitimately have an `external/` submodule.
/external/

# Coverage artifacts
.coverage*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Private/local-only docs (generic pattern — reveals no intent in the ignore list itself)
*.local.md

# ML workflow: data lives OUTSIDE the repo (paths.yaml points at it), MLflow tracking, training runs.
# Anchored to root (`/data/`, not `data/`) so a source package like core/data/ isn't silently
# untracked, hiding its tests (bd hhy).
/data/
/paths.yaml
/runs/
/mlruns/

# Beads / Dolt engine bits (issues.jsonl is tracked; the embedded engine is not)
.dolt/
.beads/*.db
.beads-credential-key

# jscpd (node) — pulled transiently by npx for the duplication gate
node_modules/

# Kaggle kit staging: the zip dir the REST upload needs. The kit ITSELF now builds under the data
# root, out of the repo - it is ~200 MB of weights and wheels, and while it lived at comp/kit it
# put a stale copy of kneemri inside the type checker's scope. verify_kit.py keeps it honest.
/comp/kit_staging/
# Trained member weights: 85 MB each. They belong in a Kaggle dataset, not in git. The manifest used to
# be tracked beside them as the reproducible description of what was packaged — but the roster is that
# description, and tracking the manifest meant tracking a second members directory inside the repo.
# comp/members was deleted 2026-08-18 (knee-n0w0); the package lives under the processed root.

# A training run's own outputs, wherever it was pointed: the checkpoint, the periodic save beside it,
# the held-out predictions and the epoch log. `arm_smoke --smoke <dir>` deletes what IT wrote, but the
# obvious directory to hand it is `experiments/arms`, whose .sh recipes ARE tracked — so a `git add -A`
# mid-sweep otherwise stages half a sweep's artifacts. Recipes in git, results out of it.
*.pt
*.partial
*.holdout.npz
*.metrics.jsonl

# .claude/inbox/ is MY mailbox — what other agents send HERE. Letters and their archive are messages,
# not source. watch.sh and the README are tracked; nothing that lands in the box ever is.
/.claude/inbox/*.txt
/.claude/inbox/read/

# .agent-runtime/inbox/ is the Kimi-side live mailbox (see .agent-runtime/): letters, archive,
# and listener state are runtime; AGENTS_STACK.md is generated by agent_md_sync.sh.
/.agent-runtime/inbox/
/.agent-runtime/AGENTS_STACK.md
experiments/logs/
gates.log
logs/kout/*.csv

# A pulled Kaggle leaderboard snapshot, not ours: 124 KB of third-party rows whose one useful
# cell (our efficiency row) is quoted in knee-7lyz. Data stays out of the repo.
/comp/efficiency_lb/

# kernel outputs downloaded for reading — evidence, not source
comp/kout*/
comp/fout*/
